& [IR7OperationsBoundaryImportAndInvariantReconciliationV1] is the IR7-S01 boundary map for operations dry-run request simulator planning
  + [boundary_map_id] is ir7-operations-boundary-import-and-invariant-reconciliation-v1
  + [boundary_map_uuid] is dae09e31-b6a6-44ab-b895-0126247a56aa
  + [slice_id] is IR7-S01
  + [source_chunk] is IR7 operations dry-run request simulator planning
  + [authority_scope] is imported operations safety contracts, imported IR6 coordination proof, post-IR6 readiness gates, operation request non-authority ladder, dry-run-only boundary, human approval limits, stale triggers, and forbidden mutation boundaries
  + [implementation_scope] is boundary import and invariant reconciliation only
  + [model_route_used] is requires deeper reasoning

  = must: import accepted operations safety, dry-run, resource safety, live-control prohibition, and IR6 coordination proof boundaries before defining IR7 request, result, refusal, fixture, implementation, or activation contracts
  = must: preserve operation requests as reviewable records, not commands
  = must: preserve dry-run results as simulation evidence, not live approval
  = must: preserve human approval records as explicit, fresh, scoped, revocable safety inputs, not blanket live-control permission
  = must: preserve IR6 coordination proof so claims, mailbox carriers, human overrides, conflict reviews, completion gates, and carrier state cannot become dispatch or operations authority
  - never: implement operations simulator code, execute commands, control processes, control GPU, mutate model runtime, dispatch jobs, access or mutate credentials, mutate network exposure, perform destructive filesystem actions, create persistent operations automation, install dependencies, mutate package metadata, dispatch agents, authorize operations control, or authorize live machine control in this slice

