& [ReconciledIR7InvariantSet] is the reconciled invariant set for IR7 operations dry-run request simulator planning
  + [invariant] is SOP source documents, accepted canonical specifications, accepted packs, accepted proofs, accepted completion reviews, accepted human override records, and SJS-signed artifacts remain source authority
  + [invariant] is operation requests describe intended effects and safety context but cannot perform effects
  + [invariant] is dry-run results simulate, classify, estimate, refuse, or require review but cannot approve live effects
  + [invariant] is refusal records preserve evidence and block unsafe operation requests as records, not commands
  + [invariant] is authority_notice, freshness_state, intended_effect, resource_target, risk_classification, blast_radius, rollback_or_abort_route, credential_boundary_ref, network_boundary_ref, human_approval_ref, and completion_review_ref are required before an operation request can become trusted dry-run input
  + [invariant] is unknown, ambiguous, credential-touching, network-touching, destructive, process, GPU, model-runtime, and job-queue targets route to high-risk review or refusal
  + [invariant] is human approval must be explicit, fresh, scoped to intended_effect and resource_target, revocable, and tied to rollback_or_abort_route
  + [invariant] is broad standing approval, stale approval, fixture success, dry-run success, projected user intent, mailbox notice, active claim, or carrier state cannot authorize live control
  + [invariant] is coordination claims coordinate work boundaries only and cannot dispatch jobs, run commands, mutate resources, or accept completion for operations effects
  + [invariant] is live-control escalation requires separate future source preservation, SJS processing, least-privilege credential boundary, rollback proof, explicit human approval rules, monitoring and abort routes, and completion review

  = must: preserve these invariants through IR7-S02 through IR7-S06
  = must: route invariant contradictions through completion review and rebake rather than silent edits

& [OperationsAuthorityLadder: IR7] is the authority ladder that all downstream IR7 projections must preserve
  + [authority_tier] is source_authority
  + [source_authority_member] is preserved source specification
  + [source_authority_member] is accepted canonical specification
  + [source_authority_member] is accepted SJS satisfaction signature
  + [source_authority_member] is accepted proof pack
  + [source_authority_member] is accepted completion review
  + [source_authority_member] is explicit accepted human override record with authority notice
  + [authority_tier] is operations_planning_record
  + [operations_planning_record_member] is operation_request
  + [operations_planning_record_member] is dry_run_result
  + [operations_planning_record_member] is refusal_record
  + [operations_planning_record_member] is resource_safety_review
  + [operations_planning_record_member] is human_approval_record
  + [authority_tier] is coordination_boundary_record
  + [coordination_boundary_record_member] is coordination_claim
  + [coordination_boundary_record_member] is mailbox_carrier_context
  + [coordination_boundary_record_member] is conflict_review_context
  + [authority_tier] is generated_projection_evidence
  + [generated_projection_evidence_member] is generated dry-run projection
  + [generated_projection_evidence_member] is generated report
  + [generated_projection_evidence_member] is fixture output
  + [authority_tier] is carrier_context
  + [carrier_context_member] is terminal output
  + [carrier_context_member] is chat message
  + [carrier_context_member] is Codex thread state
  + [carrier_context_member] is mailbox path
  + [carrier_context_member] is UI event

  = must: display lower authority tier and trust limit anywhere lower-tier records may influence action
  = must: prevent lower tiers from satisfying live-control, source-authority, completion, or dispatch obligations without separate accepted authority

& [IR7GeneratedOutputAndFixtureBoundary] is the generated-output and fixture boundary for IR7-S01
  + [fixture_file_creation_authorized] is false
  + [expected_ledger_creation_authorized] is false
  + [generated_output_creation_authorized] is false
  + [future_fixture_slice] is IR7-S04 after IR7-S01 through IR7-S03 acceptance
  + [future_generated_output_policy_slice] is IR7-S05 after IR7-S04 acceptance
  + [current_generated_output_role] is none_created_by_this_slice
  + [future_generated_output_default_authority] is non_authoritative_projection_only

  = must: reject IR7-S01 completion if fixture sources, expected ledgers, generated output files, dry-run reports, carrier caches, or projection reports are created
  = must: require later accepted generated-output policy before any generated operations projection root can be trusted even as disposable evidence

& [ForbiddenIR7S01MutationList] is the forbidden mutation set for IR7-S01
  + [forbidden_mutation] is editing accepted FSC5, IR6, post-IR6, or IR7 authority inputs to make reconciliation easier
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating operation requests as commands
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating dry-run results as live approval
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating human approval requests or broad approval as live-control permission
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating coordination claims, mailbox carriers, or conflict reviews as dispatch authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing operations simulator code
  + [forbidden_mutation] is creating fixture source files
  + [forbidden_mutation] is creating expected ledger files
  + [forbidden_mutation] is creating generated output files
  + [forbidden_mutation] is installing dependencies or mutating package metadata
  + [forbidden_mutation] is executing commands
  + [forbidden_mutation] is starting, stopping, killing, or reprioritizing live processes
  + [forbidden_mutation] is launching, cancelling, or scheduling GPU workloads
  + [forbidden_mutation] is starting, stopping, installing, upgrading, or configuring model runtimes
  + [forbidden_mutation] is dispatching or cancelling jobs
  + [forbidden_mutation] is accessing, writing, rotating, or mutating credentials or secrets
  + [forbidden_mutation] is opening, exposing, or mutating network listeners or firewall state
  + [forbidden_mutation] is performing destructive filesystem actions
  + [forbidden_mutation] is creating persistent operations automation
  + [forbidden_mutation] is authorizing operations control or live machine control

  = must: fail IR7-S01 review if any forbidden mutation appears in the output

& [DownstreamStaleTriggerList: IR7] is the stale trigger set for downstream IR7 work
  + [stale_trigger] is IR7 canonical specification hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR7 final slice surface changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR7 minting review changes
  + [stale_trigger] is post-IR6 readiness surface changes
  + [stale_trigger] is FSC5 operations safety pack hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is operations safety canonical hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is FSC5 operations boundary, dry-run, resource safety, or live-control prohibition contract changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR6 implementation proof pack hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR6 implementation completion review changes
  + [stale_trigger] is dry-run output treated as live approval
  + [stale_trigger] is human approval display treated as live-control permission
  + [stale_trigger] is operation-like projection treated as command execution, job dispatch, process control, GPU control, model runtime mutation, credential mutation, network mutation, destructive filesystem action, operations control, or live-control effect

  = must: mark affected downstream slices stale when any listed trigger fires
  = must: route stale-trigger repair through completion review and rebake rather than silent edits

